# Media goes to Git LFS, and it has to be set up BEFORE the first image lands.
#
# A png committed normally is a blob in the history forever: every clone pays
# for it, and taking it out again means rewriting history that other checkouts
# have already pulled. This file is cheap insurance against that, and it is
# only insurance if it precedes the media.
#
# The site's media is screenshots of the interface and a console recording
# (SQU-148), and the demo's assets (SQU-183). Text stays in git: Markdown,
# JSON fixtures, the OpenAPI document and SVG, which is text and diffs.
*.png  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gif  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.cast filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# The demo ships two built interfaces under docs/demo/, and each carries its
# webfonts. Fonts are binary and never diff; they belong with the images. The
# built JavaScript stays in git as text -- it is large but it diffs, and a
# demo rebuilt from a new tag should arrive as a reviewable change.
*.woff  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.woff2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ttf   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
